# Omit Nuxt Auto-Imported Symbols

Nuxt auto-imports these in app/layer code — **do not import them**:

- **Vue APIs:** `ref`, `computed`, `reactive`, `watch`, `watchEffect`, `onMounted`, `nextTick`, …
- **Nuxt composables:** `useRoute`, `useRouter`, `navigateTo`, `useState`, `useNuxtApp`, `useRuntimeConfig`, `useFetch`, `useAsyncData`, `useSeoMeta`, `definePageMeta`, …
- **Components (incl. Nuxt UI `U*`):** use directly in the template — no `#components` / `@nuxt/ui` import.

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
// ❌ redundant — all three are auto-imported
import { computed } from 'vue'
import { UButton } from '#components'
const route = useRoute()
</script>
<template>
  <UButton :to="route.path" /> <!-- ✅ no import needed -->
</template>
```

## Exception: Types Are Not Auto-Imported

Type-only imports are fine and often required — keep them:

- **Component prop types** — derive from the component with a **type-only**
  `#components` import:
  ```ts
  import type { UButton } from '#components'
  type UButtonProps = InstanceType<typeof UButton>['$props']
  ```
- **Vue type helpers** (`Ref`, `ComputedRef`, `PropType`) still need
  `import type { … } from 'vue'`.

## Exception: Portable / Engine Code

`.ts` written to be framework-portable or extractable may import Vue APIs from
`vue` explicitly on purpose — don't strip those.

## IDE Note

If the IDE reports `Cannot find name 'computed'`, run **`nuxt prepare`** or
**`pnpm dev`** so `.nuxt/imports.d.ts` exists.
